# At the workshop: paste the two WORKSHOP_ lines from the /code page of the workshop site; that is how a run reaches your map.
# At home, or after the event: put your Deepgram API key after DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=.
# make setup copies this file to .env, which Git ignores. Every line is KEY=value, no quotes, no spaces around the =; the rest of the rules are in docs/troubleshooting.md.

# A workshop token runs your program through the workshop agent and covers every
# mission, including 01 and 02, which use `timing`. Get it at
# https://workshops.deepgram.com/builders-lab/code (Get a code-project token) and
# paste the two lines it shows here; WORKSHOP_URL is
# wss://workshops.deepgram.com/builders-lab/sdk. With both lines set (and
# DEEPGRAM_AGENT_URL empty), the token is used, even if a DEEPGRAM_API_KEY is set
# too. A token lasts 8 hours or until the workshop live agent closes, whichever
# comes first. After the event, set DEEPGRAM_API_KEY and leave WORKSHOP_TOKEN empty.
WORKSHOP_URL=
WORKSHOP_TOKEN=

# Your Deepgram API key, for make run and make live. Runs on it stay off your
# map. Free key:
# https://console.deepgram.com/signup (create one under API Keys). Paste it with
# no quotes or spaces. make check runs offline and needs no key.
DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=

# The listen model for every mission but 04. Empty: nova-3 (v1), which runs on
# every Deepgram project. The workshop site uses flux-general-en (v2); set both
# lines to match it. With a workshop token and these empty, flux-general-en is used.
LISTEN_MODEL=
LISTEN_VERSION=

# Mission 03 stretch: the `thinking` model id, on a Deepgram project that has the
# `thinking` feature. If it runs on its own agent endpoint, that goes in
# DEEPGRAM_AGENT_URL (with a workshop token, leave that empty). When it is set,
# mission 03 asks for the `thinking` provider in its Settings. Think models:
# https://developers.deepgram.com/reference/voice-agent/think-models
THINKING_MODEL=

# The Voice Agent endpoint. Leave empty: that is Deepgram production
# (wss://agent.deepgram.com). A wss:// host (wss://agent.example.com) or the full
# wss://.../v1/agent/converse URL both work. It starts with wss:// (ws:// is accepted
# too, for the local check harness only). An address that names a host is dialed, not
# checked: a wrong one stops with a Could not reach the agent line.
DEEPGRAM_AGENT_URL=
